Use Mono.deferContextual + .contextWrite(ReactiveSecurityContextHolder.withAuthentication(...)).

Add three tests: 
  @Test void login_redisCheckFails_failsOpen_proceedsToAuth() { when(redisTemplate.opsForValue().get(EMAIL_KEY)).thenReturn(Mono.error(new RuntimeException("redis down"))); when(redisTemplate.opsForValue().get(IP_KEY)).thenReturn(Mono.empty()); // user found, password matches → expect successful login (or at least non-429 outcome). } 
